# AnalogAtlas environment variables (example/template)
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your real credentials/keys.
# Do NOT commit `.env` with secrets. (`.env` is gitignored; `.env.example` is tracked.)

# --- NASA Earthdata Login (required for authenticated downloads via earthaccess) ---
# Create a free account: https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov/
# Use either username/password OR a token.
EARTHDATA_USERNAME=
EARTHDATA_PASSWORD=
# EARTHDATA_TOKEN=

# --- ESA Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem (optional, for Sentinel-1/2 access) ---
# https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/
# COPERNICUS_CLIENT_ID=
# COPERNICUS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# COPERNICUS_USERNAME=
# COPERNICUS_PASSWORD=

# --- JAXA G-Portal (optional, for G-Portal product access) ---
# https://gportal.jaxa.jp/gpr/
# JAXA_GPORTAL_USERNAME=
# JAXA_GPORTAL_PASSWORD=

# How it's used (web folder):
# - Copy this file to `.env` in the same folder (web/.env) and fill in real values.
# - Scripts in web/scripts auto-load `web/.env` (see `scripts/env.py`).
#   From the web/ folder run:
#     python -m venv .venv
#     .venv\Scripts\pip install -r scripts/requirements.txt
#     .venv\Scripts\python scripts/retrieve_data.py
#   This verifies NASA endpoints and fetches verified NASA ODE product/metadata records into data/verified_sources/.
# - For real Earthdata downloads, credentials are read from env by earthaccess in your ETL:
#     import earthaccess; earthaccess.login()  # uses EARTHDATA_* from web/.env
#   Download raw data to data/raw/ and produce processed outputs in data/processed/ and/or public/data/.
# - These are SECRET backend credentials: do NOT use `VITE_` prefix and do NOT access them in browser code.
#   The Vite web app must never expose Earthdata/Copernicus/JAXA keys client-side.
#
# Notes:
# - Earthdata credentials enable real EO downloads/ETL (MODIS, SMAP, MERRA-2, ASTER, ICESat-2, NASADEM, etc.)
#   to replace synthetic Earth feature data. See docs/DATA_SOURCES.md and docs/NASA_SOURCE_VERIFICATION.md.
# - Keep this file as placeholders only; put actual values in `.env`.